WEBVTT

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:02.118
- Previously on The O.C.:
- This is school?

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:06.379
If you graduate from here, you can
get into any college in the UC system.

00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:09.339
What happens in Mexico, you know,
stays in Mexico.

00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:11.049
You don't deserve her.

00:00:11.257 --> 00:00:13.050
- I didn't want to kill myself.
- I know.

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:15.676
- I'm so sorry about everything.
- Go away.

00:00:15.885 --> 00:00:19.304
- Our chemistry is undeniable.
- I don't have a date to the cotillion.

00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:20.888
Would you be my escort?

00:00:21.055 --> 00:00:23.807
- Good news! I'm available.
- No.

00:00:24.015 --> 00:00:26.308
- Who's Rachel?
- She works at the law firm I met with.

00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:28.976
- So if I did take this job...
- You already have.

00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:31.019
- This is Rachel.
- I'm Rachel.

00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:33.104
You and Marissa want different things.

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:36.690
- You don't know what she wants!
- She doesn't want to live with you.

00:00:36.898 --> 00:00:39.983
I wanna live with Dad.
At least for now.

00:00:40.192 --> 00:00:41.776
Ryan's had a lot to overcome.

00:00:41.985 --> 00:00:44.653
- Not exactly Harbor School material.
- Give me a shot.

00:00:57.494 --> 00:00:59.912
First day of school. Excited?

00:01:02.581 --> 00:01:07.000
You know, I ask you questions in
the hopes of eliciting an actual response.

00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:10.169
- I feel I convey more with a look.
- You look adorable.

00:01:10.377 --> 00:01:11.753
- No.
- Cute?

00:01:11.962 --> 00:01:14.505
- Dope? Rad?
- Please, this is so painful!

00:01:14.713 --> 00:01:16.006
I'm sorry.

00:01:16.214 --> 00:01:18.758
- How was surfing?
- Cut it short.

00:01:18.966 --> 00:01:21.634
I wanted to see the boys off.

00:01:21.843 --> 00:01:24.553
Doesn't Seth look rad?

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.680
Oh, you do look rad! Mad props, son.

00:01:28.889 --> 00:01:31.474
Thank God. Are you ready to go?

00:01:31.682 --> 00:01:33.684
First day. You excited?

00:01:33.892 --> 00:01:35.685
Enough said.

00:01:35.893 --> 00:01:39.354
How do you do that? How do you
convey everything with just a look?

00:01:39.562 --> 00:01:41.021
And again.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.649
- How are you doing? Nervous?
- Why would I be nervous?

00:01:44.857 --> 00:01:47.359
Because we're going to school
with, like, 300 Lukes...

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.610
...minus the redeeming social qualities.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.114
I got it. Sorry.
You meant you were nervous.

00:01:56.156 --> 00:01:59.116
- Don't be nervous.
- I'm not nervous. I'm just not going.

00:01:59.325 --> 00:02:01.784
You have to go. You own the school.

00:02:01.993 --> 00:02:04.161
What about Kickoff Carnival?
You're the social chair.

00:02:04.494 --> 00:02:07.121
Let's see. Be humiliated
in front of the entire school...

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.664
...or hire someone
to do balloon animals?

00:02:09.873 --> 00:02:12.208
Hire the guy who makes
the balloon octopus.

00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:17.086
So your boyfriend cheated on you,
and, yes, you almost died in Mexico.

00:02:17.294 --> 00:02:19.004
And the scandal with your dad...

00:02:19.212 --> 00:02:21.505
If you're trying
to make me feel better...

00:02:21.714 --> 00:02:25.841
Okay. The point is, there's
no such thing as bad publicity.

00:02:26.925 --> 00:02:29.969
- Is that something burning?
- Okay, so...

00:02:30.177 --> 00:02:35.222
...new oven. Haven't quite figured out
how to make French toast.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.015
Not in the oven
would be a good place to start.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.309
Since no one will hire me,
I've got plenty of time...

00:02:41.518 --> 00:02:43.894
...I'm gonna go out and buy a cookbook.

00:02:44.103 --> 00:02:46.896
Come on! It's good, they're crunchy.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.648
- See?
- No, thanks.

00:02:50.857 --> 00:02:53.525
I don't know who I'm more
worried about here.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:59.154
I think it's safe to say that
this year is going to be different.

00:03:00.363 --> 00:03:04.324
- Maybe this year will be different.
- That's the mantra every year.

00:03:04.532 --> 00:03:08.910
And every year some big water-polo
player pees in one of my shoes.

00:03:09.118 --> 00:03:13.496
Just kidding. They pee in both.
Ryan has Mr. Schmidt for pre-calc.

00:03:14.872 --> 00:03:18.833
- What's wrong with Mr. Schmidt?
- Nothing. Say hi to his mole for me.

00:03:19.041 --> 00:03:21.167
At least you have each other.

00:03:21.376 --> 00:03:24.836
- Very wise, Dad.
- Thank you, son.

00:03:25.378 --> 00:03:26.629
We're doomed.

00:04:08.155 --> 00:04:12.700
The master race has been perfected
and they all go to our school.

00:04:14.826 --> 00:04:16.202
Hey, fellas.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.330
All right, don't get
your Speedos in a bunch.

00:04:21.538 --> 00:04:24.207
- This is a nightmare.
- This is a nightmare.

00:04:24.374 --> 00:04:27.876
- I bet, like, no one even knows.
- Are you kidding?

00:04:28.084 --> 00:04:31.420
- I heard she died down there.
- She looks pretty good for a dead girl.

00:04:31.628 --> 00:04:35.214
Hey, whores!
Why don't you go work another corner.

00:04:35.422 --> 00:04:39.341
Summ, maybe I should go home.
Help my dad unpack.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.969
Coop, that is as bad as it's gonna get.
I spoke too soon.

00:04:43.177 --> 00:04:46.721
Hello, Summer. What does
your schedule look like today?

00:04:46.929 --> 00:04:48.972
- Full.
- Really?

00:04:49.181 --> 00:04:51.224
- A friendly face.
- How's it going?

00:04:51.432 --> 00:04:53.225
- Not good. You?
- Worse.

00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:58.395
So why don't we just get out of here?
Right now. Go down to the pier.

00:04:58.603 --> 00:05:01.855
I can't. Dean Kim would call my dad.
Or worse, my mom.

00:05:02.064 --> 00:05:06.525
- Okay. How about after school?
- I'm chairing the carnival committee.

00:05:06.692 --> 00:05:11.069
- I know. I've been looking for an excuse.
- I think you found one.

00:05:11.236 --> 00:05:13.988
- I'll meet you out front.
- Something to look forward to.

00:05:14.155 --> 00:05:16.823
Coop! Can we go, please?

00:05:20.158 --> 00:05:22.702
Hey. Could we maybe talk or...?

00:05:24.953 --> 00:05:26.662
Stay away from her.

00:05:26.829 --> 00:05:28.914
How?
We all go to the same school.

00:05:29.122 --> 00:05:30.748
You should've thought about that...

00:05:30.957 --> 00:05:34.292
...before hooking up with one
of her best friends! Ass!

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:41.505
- You okay?
- Yeah. I just have to get used to it.

00:05:42.339 --> 00:05:43.798
This, I guess.

00:05:45.007 --> 00:05:48.968
- But we're still on, right?
- Yeah. Something to look forward to.

00:05:51.011 --> 00:05:52.679
Coop!

00:05:52.887 --> 00:05:54.930
See you, Summer.

00:05:56.598 --> 00:05:59.516
Slowly I thaw her icy heart.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:04.811
- Look at you.
- Lf I must.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:10.440
- New suit. New scent. New look.
- I feel like this is heading somewhere.

00:06:10.607 --> 00:06:12.566
- New girlfriend.
- And there it is.

00:06:12.775 --> 00:06:14.234
You're still all bent out of...

00:06:19.862 --> 00:06:25.533
Oh, God! I should've found
an attractive co-worker years ago.

00:06:25.741 --> 00:06:28.201
- It was a figure of speech.
- Rachel's attractive?

00:06:28.409 --> 00:06:30.452
Is that her name? It's context.

00:06:30.661 --> 00:06:34.872
Only, you know, in relation to which
she invokes amorous feelings...

00:06:35.039 --> 00:06:38.958
...in my far more, extremely more,
attractive wife.

00:06:40.417 --> 00:06:42.418
Good answer.

00:06:51.299 --> 00:06:54.384
- Mornings used to be our time.
- I remember them well.

00:06:54.592 --> 00:06:56.385
What happened?

00:07:02.222 --> 00:07:06.266
Work happened.
Just hang on one sec.

00:07:06.475 --> 00:07:10.060
Wait a minute. I can't get it.
Hang on one sec.

00:07:11.603 --> 00:07:14.355
Just hold on. I got it.

00:07:14.522 --> 00:07:15.772
Wait.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:21.943
How did she know?
You're not gonna answer it, are you?

00:07:27.863 --> 00:07:30.115
It's my dad.

00:07:32.991 --> 00:07:35.118
Hey, Rachel.

00:07:35.326 --> 00:07:36.869
Hi, Dad.

00:07:37.077 --> 00:07:40.830
So if you'd care to join me
for lunch today...

00:07:41.038 --> 00:07:42.914
...I can arrange for an empty chair.

00:07:43.123 --> 00:07:45.583
There's nothing but empty chairs
at your table.

00:07:45.791 --> 00:07:47.084
Seth Cohen?

00:07:48.209 --> 00:07:50.961
Anna! Hey, how are you doing?

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:53.046
Excuse me, we were talking here.

00:07:53.254 --> 00:07:56.423
So insulting him
counts as conversation?

00:07:56.631 --> 00:08:00.926
If it doesn't, then we've never spoken.
Remember Anna from Pittsburgh?

00:08:01.092 --> 00:08:05.762
- How could I forget?
- We're still on for lunch today, right?

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:09.473
- She probably didn't even hear me.
- Seth, what are you doing?

00:08:09.681 --> 00:08:12.433
I thought you got past
this whole Summer thing at cotillion.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.977
Right. And I know it seems like
not a lot of progress has been made...

00:08:16.185 --> 00:08:19.687
...but I have to tell you... Yeah, not that
much progress has been made.

00:08:19.854 --> 00:08:24.899
Despite all my best judgments,
I cannot not like her.

00:08:25.107 --> 00:08:27.776
- You're such a boy.
- Well, whatever.

00:08:27.984 --> 00:08:33.237
- I'm nothing but available for that girl.
- All right. Right there.

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:37.907
That's your problem. Girls like to be
chased by guys that aren't into them.

00:08:38.115 --> 00:08:40.200
That sounds a little bit
like a game to me...

00:08:40.409 --> 00:08:42.702
...and I don't really like to play games.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.412
Unless we're talking about
Saturday-night Jenga...

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.705
...a little Magic: The Gathering.
I love Magic: The Gathering.

00:08:48.914 --> 00:08:51.957
Maybe you just don't know how to play.

00:08:52.166 --> 00:08:55.293
- Well, you're a girl, right?
- Yeah.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.961
- And we're friends, right?
- Sure.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.421
Then train me in the ways of women.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.422
I don't understand chicks like Summer.

00:09:02.631 --> 00:09:04.424
I'll teach you how to play Jenga.

00:09:05.508 --> 00:09:08.718
- You really like her?
- Since I was 10.

00:09:10.052 --> 00:09:11.428
Fine.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.223
- But I make no promises.
- Trust me, I cannot do any worse.

00:09:17.765 --> 00:09:19.391
That I trust.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.143
You're my girl.

00:09:23.519 --> 00:09:25.353
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:09:25.562 --> 00:09:28.522
What were you doing this morning
when I called? You sounded...

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:29.981
Did I wake you?

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:33.233
- I was spending some time with my wife.
- Yeah? How'd that go?

00:09:34.484 --> 00:09:37.569
- Well, I got to work on time.
- Too bad.

00:09:37.778 --> 00:09:41.030
It might be a while before your wife
is in the mood for love.

00:09:41.238 --> 00:09:43.531
Yeah? Something you know I don't?

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:47.284
I know lots that you don't,
but in this case...

00:09:47.492 --> 00:09:49.577
...are you familiar
with the Balboa Wetlands?

00:09:49.785 --> 00:09:51.953
Yeah, the largest coastal wetlands
in California.

00:09:52.162 --> 00:09:56.581
Home to the blue heron,
the brown pelican and the swamp rose.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.040
Right.

00:09:58.249 --> 00:10:01.209
The wetlands are key
to water quality in the county.

00:10:01.418 --> 00:10:05.337
- Not to mention, they're kind of pretty.
- Naturally, they must be destroyed.

00:10:05.545 --> 00:10:09.297
The Balboa Heights are 250 acres
of land that sit above said wetlands.

00:10:09.506 --> 00:10:12.883
- Every developer's after the Heights.
- Somebody got it.

00:10:13.092 --> 00:10:16.510
And they're looking to tear it up,
put in condos, a golf course.

00:10:16.719 --> 00:10:20.596
Thank God. The lack of golf courses
around here, it's tragic.

00:10:20.805 --> 00:10:24.307
This is a policy-changing,
career-making piece of litigation.

00:10:24.515 --> 00:10:29.644
A tree-hugging crusader, like yourself,
would kill for a case like this.

00:10:29.852 --> 00:10:32.520
- And you want to share this with me.
- Yes.

00:10:32.687 --> 00:10:34.146
Why?

00:10:41.443 --> 00:10:44.736
Oh, my wife's company is the plaintiff.

00:10:44.945 --> 00:10:47.238
It's her father's company.

00:10:49.031 --> 00:10:50.823
Why even tempt me with this?

00:10:51.032 --> 00:10:54.117
It's a conflict of interest.
I'm not even sure it'd be ethical.

00:10:54.326 --> 00:10:58.203
The client, the Balboa Land Trust,
not only waived the conflict of interest...

00:10:58.412 --> 00:11:01.080
...they insisted you take the case.

00:11:01.247 --> 00:11:05.458
Your politics, your passion,
your dislike for your father-in-law.

00:11:05.624 --> 00:11:09.502
- You're the ideal advocate.
- My wife will have a different spin on it.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.086
You came to this firm...

00:11:11.295 --> 00:11:14.296
...because we have the resources
to help you make a difference.

00:11:14.505 --> 00:11:18.632
They're gonna teach this in law school.
So, what's it gonna be?

00:11:18.799 --> 00:11:21.634
Your sex life? Or the swamp rose?

00:11:35.059 --> 00:11:38.687
Did you know that
she overdosed on Vicodin?

00:12:07.455 --> 00:12:10.123
You are not quitting your post
as social chair, Marissa.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.750
You were elected by the students,
you've held the position for two years.

00:12:13.959 --> 00:12:18.003
I know, Dr. Kim. But that was before
everything that happened this summer.

00:12:18.211 --> 00:12:21.505
I understand you are going
through a lot of change right now...

00:12:21.714 --> 00:12:24.882
...but you're a leader here at Harbor,
that doesn't have to change.

00:12:25.091 --> 00:12:28.468
You're a wonderful example.
Students look up to you.

00:12:28.676 --> 00:12:30.177
Not anymore.

00:12:30.386 --> 00:12:34.847
Putting aside the issue of how walking
away from your responsibilities...

00:12:35.014 --> 00:12:38.349
...will affect your college transcript...

00:12:38.557 --> 00:12:42.393
...people are always going to talk.

00:12:42.602 --> 00:12:46.646
You may as well give them
something good to talk about.

00:12:46.813 --> 00:12:50.732
Don't disappear, Marissa.
This is your school, your life.

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:52.858
Your future.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.486
Hey, what are you doing?

00:12:57.653 --> 00:12:59.445
You never told me
about summer reading.

00:12:59.654 --> 00:13:00.905
Who does summer reading?

00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:05.408
- Apparently, everyone in my class.
- Oh. Yeah. Sorry about that one.

00:13:05.574 --> 00:13:08.785
Anna here has convinced me
to join The Plank, the literary magazine.

00:13:08.993 --> 00:13:11.953
I needed an extracurricular activity,
and apparently...

00:13:12.162 --> 00:13:14.205
...you don't have to wear a
sports bra.

00:13:14.413 --> 00:13:16.873
It's appealing on many levels.
Plus I feel...

00:13:17.082 --> 00:13:19.750
...I have a few limericks
to share with the world.

00:13:19.917 --> 00:13:22.460
Have fun.
I'm gonna hang with Marissa.

00:13:22.668 --> 00:13:24.961
School might not suck this year.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:29.297
Hey. I have to plan
this carnival thing after all.

00:13:29.464 --> 00:13:31.257
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah.

00:13:31.465 --> 00:13:33.425
I talked to the dean, and...

00:13:33.634 --> 00:13:37.344
...I think getting involved in school again
might not be a bad idea.

00:13:38.512 --> 00:13:41.805
- I know, that sounds lame.
- Yeah. No, it's cool.

00:13:42.014 --> 00:13:45.099
- So...
- Can we reschedule?

00:13:45.266 --> 00:13:47.267
- Absolutely.
- What about the carnival?

00:13:47.476 --> 00:13:50.227
I'll save you a ride on the Ferris wheel.

00:13:50.394 --> 00:13:53.771
No Ferris wheels. I don't do heights.

00:13:55.147 --> 00:13:59.441
- But we'll figure something out.
- Are you sure you're gonna be...?

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:03.861
I'm fine. I just got a lot of reading to do.
Like 500 years of it.

00:14:04.028 --> 00:14:06.070
Okay. So I'll see you.

00:14:31.003 --> 00:14:34.755
- Morning.
- I didn't hear you come in last night.

00:14:34.964 --> 00:14:36.840
I didn't want to wake you.
You look nice.

00:14:37.048 --> 00:14:39.800
Dad's demanding a company breakfast.
Some kind of crisis.

00:14:39.967 --> 00:14:42.969
If this is how it's gonna be,
after a couple of weeks of work...

00:14:43.177 --> 00:14:46.179
...we're gonna be like...
- Two ships passing in the morning.

00:14:46.387 --> 00:14:48.180
What have they got you working on?

00:14:48.389 --> 00:14:51.265
A big high-profile case.

00:14:51.474 --> 00:14:53.767
How about lunch today? I'll pay.

00:14:53.975 --> 00:14:55.685
No, actually, you can pay.

00:14:55.893 --> 00:14:59.062
You're the one that's working
on a high-profile case.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:00.980
How about Friday?

00:15:01.147 --> 00:15:04.440
I'll have my people call your people.
I love you.

00:15:04.649 --> 00:15:06.608
I love you too.

00:15:17.407 --> 00:15:19.199
Hey, kid.

00:15:21.284 --> 00:15:24.203
- How did school go for you?
- Fine. Just behind.

00:15:24.369 --> 00:15:26.662
After one day? Nice work.

00:15:27.913 --> 00:15:30.832
It's brutal. You're brave to face
those preppy little savages.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.291
I mean the teachers.

00:15:32.499 --> 00:15:35.877
I don't think it was a good idea,
me in private school.

00:15:36.085 --> 00:15:40.296
- You're one of their smartest kids.
- It's not the work. It's just...

00:15:40.463 --> 00:15:43.923
...everybody's got something,
except me.

00:15:44.132 --> 00:15:46.717
- Well, you got Seth.
- Seth's got his women.

00:15:48.426 --> 00:15:50.136
Seth Cohen?

00:15:51.094 --> 00:15:53.096
Okay. So...

00:15:53.304 --> 00:15:55.472
Really?

00:15:57.473 --> 00:16:00.851
So you need something.
An activity. A sport.

00:16:01.559 --> 00:16:03.686
- Ladies.
- Don Juan, we're trying to find...

00:16:03.894 --> 00:16:06.146
...an extracurricular activity for Ryan.

00:16:06.354 --> 00:16:09.189
- Okay.
- Harbor's got a great archery program...

00:16:09.356 --> 00:16:10.815
Archery, no.
Absolutely not.

00:16:10.982 --> 00:16:12.233
Fencing?

00:16:12.441 --> 00:16:16.068
What century are you in? Open your
mind. This isn't me we're talking about.

00:16:16.277 --> 00:16:19.612
With Ryan, we have an opportunity
to have a real athlete in the family.

00:16:19.821 --> 00:16:21.072
Somebody to achieve...

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:24.282
...all that your Jewishness has
prevented me from accomplishing.

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:26.783
- I always wanted to play soccer.
- I used to play.

00:16:26.992 --> 00:16:30.327
- Done.
- Glad I could help.

00:16:34.622 --> 00:16:37.373
I didn't get around
to getting those cookbooks.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:40.625
I guess it's better
to play it safe, then.

00:16:40.834 --> 00:16:43.586
So how's sleeping on the sofa?

00:16:43.752 --> 00:16:45.212
It's fine.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.880
- It's just temporary.
- I can handle it.

00:16:48.088 --> 00:16:50.131
Did you talk to your mom?

00:16:53.383 --> 00:16:55.885
I'm sorry about all this, sweetheart.

00:16:56.093 --> 00:16:59.179
- I just wish you would've told me.
- I know, I know.

00:16:59.345 --> 00:17:01.722
But things will be different now.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.515
Hey, don't get too excited.

00:17:04.724 --> 00:17:08.976
The phone company is installing
an actual phone line.

00:17:09.185 --> 00:17:11.019
A very big day.

00:17:12.562 --> 00:17:15.314
- Hey, Mr. Cooper.
- Luke.

00:17:15.481 --> 00:17:18.399
So is this your new place?
Looks great.

00:17:19.024 --> 00:17:23.027
- Not buying it, Luke.
- Right. Can I talk to Marissa?

00:17:23.194 --> 00:17:25.195
- No. You can't.
- Come on, it's me.

00:17:25.403 --> 00:17:27.071
If I could talk to her...

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:31.907
Yeah, she told me what happened,
and she doesn't want to talk right now.

00:17:32.116 --> 00:17:34.701
Come on. If anybody knows
about being in the doghouse...

00:17:34.909 --> 00:17:36.952
Don't say it.

00:17:38.412 --> 00:17:40.454
What can I do?

00:17:40.663 --> 00:17:42.789
You can leave.

00:17:44.374 --> 00:17:47.751
Well, tell her sorry.

00:17:48.876 --> 00:17:50.127
Okay.

00:17:57.924 --> 00:17:59.300
Thanks.

00:18:04.886 --> 00:18:07.096
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:18:08.097 --> 00:18:11.182
- How did it go with the carnival?
- Oh, very exciting.

00:18:11.349 --> 00:18:12.975
If I get out of my meeting early...

00:18:13.183 --> 00:18:15.476
We're voting on cotton candy
versus funnel cakes.

00:18:15.685 --> 00:18:19.270
- Cotton candy, no question.
- My thoughts exactly.

00:18:19.479 --> 00:18:23.273
But I can't today. I got soccer practice.

00:18:23.481 --> 00:18:26.316
- You do?
- Yeah, I'm gonna try out.

00:18:26.483 --> 00:18:30.361
I figure getting involved in school
might not be such a bad idea.

00:18:30.569 --> 00:18:34.947
Yeah. Plus, now we both get out
at 5, right? Meet you in the quad.

00:18:35.155 --> 00:18:37.323
See you then.

00:18:46.162 --> 00:18:49.039
- Hello. Is this seat taken?
- It is now.

00:18:49.247 --> 00:18:50.498
Cool.

00:18:56.836 --> 00:19:00.004
You can sit here
if you want, Summer.

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:02.631
Thanks.

00:19:09.885 --> 00:19:12.095
Seth, come sit here by me.

00:19:13.346 --> 00:19:16.348
Are you sure? You don't mind
one cheek on, one cheek off?

00:19:16.514 --> 00:19:18.307
Sit!

00:19:20.559 --> 00:19:22.935
Sitting.

00:19:26.604 --> 00:19:30.106
Oh, my God!
Okay, so tell me about Tahiti.

00:19:30.315 --> 00:19:33.567
- Oh, it was incredible.
- Anna just sailed to Tahiti.

00:19:33.775 --> 00:19:36.986
Sailing is, like,
so not the fastest way to get anywhere.

00:19:38.487 --> 00:19:41.322
If you'd flown,
you would've gotten there a lot sooner.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.865
You should be on the debate team.

00:19:53.996 --> 00:19:55.455
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:19:56.206 --> 00:19:58.541
- Nice office.
- It came furnished.

00:20:00.042 --> 00:20:04.920
- I brought you lunch.
- Well, it's not a lump of coal.

00:20:05.128 --> 00:20:07.338
- When were you going to tell me?
- Soon.

00:20:07.546 --> 00:20:10.173
Not soon enough.
I signed a deposition this morning.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:11.924
Oh, honey.

00:20:13.092 --> 00:20:16.052
I'm not even sure
if I'm gonna take this case.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.053
There is no case!

00:20:18.261 --> 00:20:22.055
You're talking about destroying one of
the world's most productive ecosystems.

00:20:22.264 --> 00:20:25.474
It's like selling off the rainforest
to profit a few individuals...

00:20:25.683 --> 00:20:28.226
...and asking generations
of others to pay for it.

00:20:28.434 --> 00:20:34.063
We have proposed to protect 350 acres
of wildlife refuge and a natural park.

00:20:34.271 --> 00:20:37.774
You'll still add 30% more traffic
and 10 tons of air pollution daily.

00:20:37.982 --> 00:20:41.317
Not to mention
what you'll do to the water supply.

00:20:41.526 --> 00:20:43.611
- You're gonna take this.
- No...

00:20:43.819 --> 00:20:45.612
Sandy, it isn't even ethical.

00:20:45.779 --> 00:20:47.780
I feel comfortable comparing ethics
with your father.

00:20:47.988 --> 00:20:50.990
Well, as long as you're comfortable.
I gotta go.

00:20:51.199 --> 00:20:55.410
I gotta keep this off my father's radar.
He's going to lose his mind.

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:02.122
All right, move! Don't wait for it!

00:21:02.622 --> 00:21:04.332
Hey. You Atwood?

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.833
- What position you coming out for?
- Striker.

00:21:07.042 --> 00:21:11.253
You see that kid out front?
That's Luke, the captain and striker.

00:21:13.754 --> 00:21:15.631
Let's go! Show me something!

00:21:16.673 --> 00:21:20.133
Hey, Ward!
You got a little competition!

00:21:24.845 --> 00:21:27.680
Thanks.
Tomorrow we'll figure out the parking.

00:21:27.888 --> 00:21:31.599
Make sure the band's booked.
No last-second surprises.

00:21:44.899 --> 00:21:46.483
We need to talk.

00:21:46.692 --> 00:21:48.860
You do not want to hear
what I have to say.

00:21:49.068 --> 00:21:50.694
- Yes, I do.
- No.

00:21:50.861 --> 00:21:54.447
All you want is for me to tell you
that everything's okay now. It's not.

00:21:54.655 --> 00:21:56.364
I know, and I'm so sorry.

00:21:56.573 --> 00:22:00.534
I don't care how you feel
or what you're going through.

00:22:00.742 --> 00:22:03.869
- Because you didn't care about me.
- That's not true.

00:22:04.078 --> 00:22:08.455
I slept with you. Then you slept
with one of my best friends.

00:22:08.664 --> 00:22:13.417
I waited for you and you lied to me.
You humiliated me.

00:22:17.628 --> 00:22:19.087
Marissa...

00:22:24.299 --> 00:22:26.175
It's just...

00:22:28.551 --> 00:22:30.094
I'm so sorry.

00:22:32.345 --> 00:22:36.556
Do you have any idea how hard it is
to not be able to talk to you?

00:22:38.015 --> 00:22:42.060
- You think it's easy for me?
- Let's just start over.

00:22:43.936 --> 00:22:45.312
Please?

00:22:46.771 --> 00:22:49.439
I don't know what I'd do without you.

00:22:55.610 --> 00:23:00.321
Just because I ruined everything,
it doesn't mean I didn't love you...

00:23:00.529 --> 00:23:02.864
...because I did.

00:23:12.329 --> 00:23:13.788
I do.

00:23:28.755 --> 00:23:31.507
You know what the worst part is?

00:23:31.716 --> 00:23:34.592
If I hadn't caught you...

00:23:34.801 --> 00:23:36.677
...I'd still love you too.

00:23:38.261 --> 00:23:40.221
I gotta go.

00:23:56.606 --> 00:23:58.232
I know that look.

00:23:58.441 --> 00:24:03.527
I was trying to keep this from my dad,
and now it's on the front page.

00:24:06.154 --> 00:24:08.113
I thought we could settle this privately.

00:24:08.322 --> 00:24:10.990
- This was not to go to the press.
- It's your firm!

00:24:11.199 --> 00:24:14.159
And now the entire
community knows we're fighting.

00:24:16.952 --> 00:24:20.204
Well, I guess
they got the story straight.

00:24:23.081 --> 00:24:25.916
- What are you doing?
- Morning ritual, Ryan.

00:24:26.083 --> 00:24:28.918
- Coffee, bagel, Arts &amp; Leisure.
- You have a morning ritual?

00:24:29.085 --> 00:24:31.211
Something I've been crafting
for a while.

00:24:33.171 --> 00:24:34.422
So, what's up, dude?

00:24:34.630 --> 00:24:37.382
How's life? We never talk anymore.
Who are you?

00:24:37.548 --> 00:24:43.302
- We had dinner 12 hours ago.
- Fine. Keep it all bottled up.

00:24:44.178 --> 00:24:45.637
- What was that?
- Nothing.

00:24:45.845 --> 00:24:49.556
That wasn't nothing. I saw
thoughts forming and words percolating.

00:24:49.764 --> 00:24:51.557
It's just...

00:24:53.475 --> 00:24:57.144
- Never mind.
- Come on! What was that, dude?

00:24:58.061 --> 00:25:02.647
Last night, I saw Marissa with Luke.

00:25:03.731 --> 00:25:05.858
- Making out?
- Making up.

00:25:07.109 --> 00:25:09.068
Luke was crying.

00:25:10.027 --> 00:25:12.112
Luke was crying?

00:25:12.904 --> 00:25:17.573
- That doesn't sound like anything.
- It didn't sound like nothing.

00:25:17.782 --> 00:25:19.825
Looked like they were
getting back together.

00:25:20.033 --> 00:25:23.452
So ask her about it.
If nothing's going on, she'll tell you.

00:25:23.661 --> 00:25:27.872
- Do not tell him!
- Shouldn't I just be honest?

00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:32.374
Never. You guys haven't even gone
on a date yet. You'll freak him out.

00:25:32.541 --> 00:25:34.668
Trust me, what he doesn't know
won't hurt you.

00:25:40.379 --> 00:25:42.881
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:25:43.089 --> 00:25:45.841
What happened to you last night?
I tried calling.

00:25:46.050 --> 00:25:49.051
Sorry. I got slammed last night.
I'm behind.

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.053
After two days?

00:25:52.012 --> 00:25:54.138
What did you do?

00:25:55.347 --> 00:25:57.640
Nothing. My meeting went long.

00:25:58.808 --> 00:26:01.184
- How'd it go?
- Good. I think it'll be good.

00:26:02.893 --> 00:26:04.728
What did you do after?

00:26:04.936 --> 00:26:07.772
- After I couldn't find you, I went home.
- Sorry.

00:26:07.980 --> 00:26:12.024
Yeah, but you've got soccer
practice later. Maybe I'll stop by.

00:26:15.318 --> 00:26:18.862
I gotta get to class. I'll see you.

00:26:34.121 --> 00:26:37.457
- I mean, ew!
- That's my girl.

00:26:37.665 --> 00:26:40.750
- Cohen, you're a good dissector.
- Hands of a surgeon.

00:26:40.959 --> 00:26:43.335
It's decided, then.
You'll be my lab partner.

00:26:43.544 --> 00:26:45.462
You can write up the lab reports.

00:26:45.670 --> 00:26:47.963
Actually, Seth already has a partner.

00:26:49.756 --> 00:26:52.174
He's promised himself to me, right?

00:26:52.383 --> 00:26:54.509
Yes. I am betrothed.

00:26:55.927 --> 00:26:57.219
Good.

00:26:59.012 --> 00:27:03.390
She wanted to be my lab partner.
You're supposed to help me get her.

00:27:03.598 --> 00:27:06.225
Watch and learn, Cohen.

00:27:08.393 --> 00:27:10.102
Follow my lead.

00:27:10.311 --> 00:27:11.770
Scalpel!

00:27:14.855 --> 00:27:16.314
Where shall we begin?

00:27:16.898 --> 00:27:18.357
The heart.

00:27:26.487 --> 00:27:29.864
Well, Sanford, you're all anybody's
talking about around here.

00:27:30.073 --> 00:27:32.991
Did you bring me into this firm
because of this case?

00:27:33.200 --> 00:27:36.285
We didn't have this case
when we hired you. Don't worry.

00:27:36.494 --> 00:27:39.871
You've already convinced everyone
that you're really torn.

00:27:40.079 --> 00:27:42.331
This could go
to the state supreme court.

00:27:42.539 --> 00:27:46.917
Yeah. And I know I could win.
It's a question of what I'm gonna lose.

00:27:48.126 --> 00:27:51.545
Well, if your marriage
can't survive this...

00:27:52.128 --> 00:27:54.713
...what kind of marriage is it?

00:27:56.631 --> 00:28:00.300
Hey, Atwood, good!
Good! Take a shot!

00:28:00.509 --> 00:28:02.802
- All right.
- Good hold, guys.

00:28:03.677 --> 00:28:07.305
All right, let's keep it moving.
Let's go! Line up!

00:28:07.513 --> 00:28:08.764
Hi.

00:28:11.682 --> 00:28:15.643
Sorry about yesterday.
That was kind of intense.

00:28:15.852 --> 00:28:20.938
The last time I cried was when
Macaulay Culkin died in My Girl.

00:28:21.147 --> 00:28:24.315
Yeah, the bee stings.
You were a mess.

00:28:25.107 --> 00:28:27.901
Kick! All right, good, good.

00:28:28.068 --> 00:28:30.527
All right, guys, let's go.

00:28:31.862 --> 00:28:35.614
- Hey, Ward! Get over here!
- I will...

00:28:38.324 --> 00:28:40.784
Sorry, coach.
I had to tape up my ankle.

00:28:42.535 --> 00:28:43.994
Excuse me.

00:28:44.203 --> 00:28:47.955
All right, we're finally all together?
I wanna see some hustle now.

00:28:55.668 --> 00:28:58.253
Hey! Illegal!

00:29:00.671 --> 00:29:03.089
Get in my office. Right now!

00:29:04.340 --> 00:29:06.300
Don't put any weight on it.

00:29:07.009 --> 00:29:08.259
Nice job.

00:29:08.801 --> 00:29:10.136
What's your problem, dude?

00:29:23.060 --> 00:29:25.812
How was soccer?

00:29:31.274 --> 00:29:33.775
So, Pops, how's the new job?

00:29:37.403 --> 00:29:39.821
Hey, Mom, I...

00:29:41.614 --> 00:29:43.823
I'm just going to be quietly eating now.

00:30:00.459 --> 00:30:01.834
Hey.

00:30:02.585 --> 00:30:04.670
What was that about?

00:30:04.878 --> 00:30:07.004
- What?
- You attacked him.

00:30:07.213 --> 00:30:10.340
He beat me to the ball.
It was a clean tackle.

00:30:10.548 --> 00:30:13.217
- Why are you lying to me?
- Why are you lying to me?

00:30:14.092 --> 00:30:16.552
- What are you talking about?
- You and Luke.

00:30:16.760 --> 00:30:20.221
- I saw you yesterday. I heard everything.
- I didn't know what to say.

00:30:20.429 --> 00:30:21.722
Why not tell me the truth?

00:30:21.930 --> 00:30:25.516
Why didn't you just tell me,
instead of hurting him?

00:30:25.724 --> 00:30:28.851
- You're as bad as he is.
- I don't need any more lies.

00:30:29.060 --> 00:30:32.854
I didn't lie to you. What happened
was between me and Luke.

00:30:33.021 --> 00:30:37.732
- It has nothing to do with you.
- Right, it has nothing to do with me.

00:30:41.818 --> 00:30:44.278
It just isn't gonna happen.

00:30:44.486 --> 00:30:46.821
No, it's not.

00:31:06.583 --> 00:31:08.126
Your coach called.

00:31:10.294 --> 00:31:12.045
He wants to suspend you
for two games.

00:31:12.253 --> 00:31:14.088
- Great.
- He thinks you got talent.

00:31:14.463 --> 00:31:16.089
He also thinks your attitude sucks.

00:31:16.298 --> 00:31:19.633
- It does.
- Sit down and listen to me.

00:31:20.801 --> 00:31:24.761
You can stand if you want,
but you know how lawyers love to talk.

00:31:35.601 --> 00:31:38.353
You don't need this blowout
on the soccer field...

00:31:38.520 --> 00:31:41.021
...to turn into a suspension from school.

00:31:41.230 --> 00:31:43.982
- This school can do great things.
- For Seth, not me.

00:31:44.190 --> 00:31:46.858
You're angry. I know that.
I don't blame you.

00:31:47.067 --> 00:31:50.778
Every day at that school,
you're gonna run into spoiled rich kids...

00:31:50.986 --> 00:31:52.987
...whose ass you are gonna
want to kick.

00:31:53.196 --> 00:31:55.989
You've gotta find a way
to work it out right now.

00:31:56.198 --> 00:31:58.657
Let's forget about suspension.

00:31:59.575 --> 00:32:02.577
We're always one mistake
away from...

00:32:04.620 --> 00:32:06.871
...from someone taking you from us.

00:32:23.590 --> 00:32:27.217
You know, Seth was never
really big on organized sports.

00:32:28.259 --> 00:32:30.719
I'd love to see you play.

00:32:31.470 --> 00:32:34.055
Go to some of your games.

00:32:44.603 --> 00:32:48.022
And women usually find
stark brutality so romantic.

00:32:48.230 --> 00:32:50.732
- I messed up.
- Yeah, well.

00:32:50.940 --> 00:32:53.775
In my experience,
you should always apologize.

00:32:53.984 --> 00:32:57.778
Even if you've done nothing wrong,
your shoes get peed in so much less.

00:32:57.986 --> 00:33:02.114
- That was a metaphor.
- Apologize. Right. And to Luke?

00:33:02.281 --> 00:33:05.408
That crybaby? No, man.
He can drown in his own tears.

00:33:05.616 --> 00:33:07.534
They're all the same.

00:33:07.742 --> 00:33:10.828
It's too bad, because I could tell
you really liked him.

00:33:16.414 --> 00:33:17.665
Hi.

00:33:19.583 --> 00:33:22.502
- Do you mind? Can we...?
- We have to get to class. Come on.

00:33:58.566 --> 00:34:00.901
I do love Mr. Solomon Burke.

00:34:07.571 --> 00:34:08.822
Hey.

00:34:12.825 --> 00:34:14.284
I was...

00:34:14.784 --> 00:34:17.077
I was gonna bring you
a bouquet of swamp roses...

00:34:17.286 --> 00:34:19.954
...but apparently they're endangered.

00:34:22.539 --> 00:34:26.833
I'm gonna take it. I gotta. I'm sorry.

00:34:28.168 --> 00:34:30.252
It's who you married.

00:34:30.461 --> 00:34:32.420
I know.

00:34:32.629 --> 00:34:35.380
You know, I've been
pissing you off for years.

00:34:35.589 --> 00:34:37.590
Why stop now?

00:34:38.632 --> 00:34:42.927
My father, my husband...
It's gonna be a long year.

00:34:44.928 --> 00:34:46.763
Could be a couple of years.

00:34:48.639 --> 00:34:53.142
Yeah. Well, I couldn't be married
to a man who wasn't a man.

00:34:54.434 --> 00:34:56.394
I'm all man.

00:35:00.063 --> 00:35:01.689
We'll get through this.

00:35:03.273 --> 00:35:06.275
There's a reason why we're together.

00:35:07.359 --> 00:35:09.068
I have that suspicion.

00:35:11.403 --> 00:35:13.112
Okay.

00:35:13.279 --> 00:35:15.572
Okay?

00:35:15.781 --> 00:35:17.031
Okay.

00:35:17.824 --> 00:35:19.074
Okay.

00:35:28.497 --> 00:35:31.874
- The kids are at that carnival.
- I heard that rumor.

00:35:33.167 --> 00:35:36.168
- Are you getting out?
- Are you getting in?

00:35:36.919 --> 00:35:38.795
Maybe.

00:35:39.004 --> 00:35:41.130
Maybe. Okay.

00:35:43.506 --> 00:35:46.008
- Oh, my God.
- Why do you keep this thing on?

00:35:46.216 --> 00:35:48.218
Emergencies.

00:35:48.926 --> 00:35:51.762
It's my dad. And it's an emergency.

00:35:54.180 --> 00:35:55.972
Hey, Dad.

00:35:58.015 --> 00:36:00.142
Rachel, hi.

00:36:06.312 --> 00:36:09.398
- Lf only Skee-Ball were a school sport.
- A boy can dream.

00:36:09.606 --> 00:36:11.399
- Let's see you take a shot.
- I'll pass.

00:36:11.607 --> 00:36:14.859
Take one shot!
Take a shot. It's very easy.

00:36:15.068 --> 00:36:17.736
Okay? Concentrate.
Lean to the left a little bit.

00:36:17.945 --> 00:36:21.197
- Any luck finding Marissa?
- No sign of her. You guys?

00:36:21.405 --> 00:36:23.615
Nothing. We have to let
Anna concentrate...

00:36:23.823 --> 00:36:26.033
...as she dares to step up to the master.

00:36:29.493 --> 00:36:32.370
Okay. Clearly, you're a lesbian.

00:36:32.579 --> 00:36:37.498
I'm gonna go trade in my tickets
for some cash prizes.

00:36:37.707 --> 00:36:41.376
Hey, do you think I should get Summer
something? What would she like?

00:36:43.252 --> 00:36:45.253
I can figure it out.

00:36:45.462 --> 00:36:48.505
Seth doesn't understand
the whole hard-to-get strategy.

00:36:48.672 --> 00:36:51.007
- That's because he's not.
- Oh.

00:36:54.551 --> 00:36:56.927
Why are you helping him
with Summer?

00:36:57.136 --> 00:36:58.595
Why not?

00:37:00.805 --> 00:37:03.640
Seth doesn't see me that way.

00:37:03.807 --> 00:37:08.018
When he looks at Summer,
he sees lips, hair and boobs.

00:37:09.102 --> 00:37:10.978
When he looks at me, he sees...

00:37:13.479 --> 00:37:15.522
...a lab partner.

00:37:15.731 --> 00:37:18.232
- We're friends.
- And you're gonna let that slide?

00:37:20.984 --> 00:37:22.610
Anna...

00:37:24.570 --> 00:37:29.239
...guys wanna be chased by girls
who aren't interested in them.

00:37:30.156 --> 00:37:32.116
Come on!

00:37:33.283 --> 00:37:35.701
Summer, it's right here.

00:37:35.910 --> 00:37:37.369
So do girls.

00:37:37.578 --> 00:37:39.746
She's heading for the Ferris wheel.
Gotta go.

00:37:39.954 --> 00:37:41.580
Good luck.

00:37:50.878 --> 00:37:53.212
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:37:55.339 --> 00:37:59.550
Actually, I'm glad we came.
It's not half as bad as last time.

00:37:59.758 --> 00:38:03.052
- You're going with me.
- Yeah, okay. Let's go.

00:38:16.018 --> 00:38:17.811
Do you mind?

00:38:20.104 --> 00:38:22.689
Not getting involved.

00:38:23.606 --> 00:38:26.442
- What are you doing?
- I wanna talk.

00:38:33.571 --> 00:38:36.406
I thought you were afraid of heights.

00:38:36.573 --> 00:38:38.949
But this is important.

00:38:39.908 --> 00:38:41.159
Oh, boy.

00:38:41.368 --> 00:38:46.454
Look. I said some things last night,
and I just want you...

00:38:48.664 --> 00:38:50.206
Whoa.

00:38:51.249 --> 00:38:54.084
- What's going on?
- We're stopped.

00:38:54.292 --> 00:38:56.377
Why are we stopped?

00:38:56.585 --> 00:39:00.046
Keep them up there a few minutes.
Let them work it out.

00:39:00.546 --> 00:39:02.798
You are the master.

00:39:03.006 --> 00:39:05.299
Cohen, there's something
I wanna tell you.

00:39:05.508 --> 00:39:08.468
All right. More advice.
I'm ready, bring it.

00:39:31.941 --> 00:39:35.026
Was this all part of the plan?

00:39:35.902 --> 00:39:38.236
Because it looks like it's working.

00:39:39.404 --> 00:39:41.363
Yeah.

00:39:41.572 --> 00:39:44.324
It was all part of the plan.

00:39:46.408 --> 00:39:48.243
So are you gonna go?

00:39:49.202 --> 00:39:52.287
Yeah. Thank you.

00:40:04.128 --> 00:40:05.670
I got this for you.

00:40:06.462 --> 00:40:09.297
It's all I could get with my tickets.

00:40:09.464 --> 00:40:10.715
Thanks.

00:40:22.556 --> 00:40:23.932
Hi, Summer.

00:40:24.849 --> 00:40:26.391
What's going on?

00:40:27.517 --> 00:40:29.185
Coop's stuck on the Ferris wheel...

00:40:29.393 --> 00:40:32.604
...and I was looking for someone
to go on the Tilt-A-Whirl with me.

00:40:32.812 --> 00:40:35.064
I'll go on it with you.

00:40:36.439 --> 00:40:38.983
Okay. I may vomit.

00:40:40.150 --> 00:40:42.110
I like those odds.

00:40:46.279 --> 00:40:48.780
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

00:40:51.115 --> 00:40:53.242
You had to get
the cheap Ferris wheel!

00:40:53.450 --> 00:40:56.202
What kind of carnival is this, Cooper?

00:41:01.664 --> 00:41:03.039
Okay.

00:41:04.165 --> 00:41:05.541
Look...

00:41:06.250 --> 00:41:09.168
I don't talk a lot about stuff...

00:41:09.377 --> 00:41:12.212
...and I really don't trust people.

00:41:13.880 --> 00:41:15.422
But I trust you.

00:41:16.798 --> 00:41:21.343
And I want to make it, this, work.

00:41:21.551 --> 00:41:26.429
No matter what. If we ever get down,
maybe we could talk about it.

00:41:26.637 --> 00:41:29.598
- Who knows when that'll be?
- Please don't say that.

00:41:33.058 --> 00:41:35.810
Maybe you just need something
to take your mind off of it.

00:41:36.018 --> 00:41:38.311
Fifty feet in the air,
how do you expect me to...?

00:42:17.669 --> 00:42:19.045
One more time.
